:"Mr. John David Risher | CEO & Director | Age 60 | Compensation: $2.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $1.6M ranks in the top quartile among Technology peers, with revenue growing 10%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $82K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Lyft, Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $6.4B market cap on $6.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +16% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -3234% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","Accruals are elevated at +18.6% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -9.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 7.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Accruals elevated at +18.6% of assets \u2014 Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (21.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Technology peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 10% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 3179% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":31.786236405776428},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"David Nierenberg's Top Q3 2026 Move: Criteo SA at a -9.55% Portfolio Impact","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/david-nierenbergs-top-q3-2026-170044171.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794589244.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.778,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"15 Dead End Jobs To Avoid at All Costs","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/15-dead-end-jobs-avoid-150000000.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794586093.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.863,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Form Energy Adds Meta and Tesla Veterans Lori Goler and Jon McNeill to Board as It Ramps Production for Commercial Growth","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/energy/articles/form-energy-adds-meta-tesla-150000589.html","date":"2026-11-13","timesta